  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A growing fiscal burden on external supporters increases expected future government borrowing and issuance to fund military and humanitarian assistance, directly lifting long-term sovereign yields through higher supply and weaker fiscal metrics.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_inflation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_support_burden" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::maritime_chokepoints_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained fiscal and material strain on Western and allied backers forces reallocation and reduced availability of naval patrols, escorts and maintenance funding for Gulf deployments, lowering the effective operational throughput and safe-transit capacity of chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
