  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A higher measured risk that the Russia–Ukraine conflict will escalate or spill over raises strategic uncertainty regionally, prompting India and China (and other BRICS pairs) to increase military readiness and diplomatic distrust, thereby elevating bilateral tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_china_india</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_spillover_ris" target="global_bond_inflation::financial_conditions_ind" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher risk of geographic or institutional spillover drives wider credit spreads, higher volatility and reduced risk appetite, tightening the composite financial conditions indicator as funding costs and constraints increase.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_inflation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_spillover_ris" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::shipping_risk_premium" id="0">
