<edge source="brics_china_india::trade_investment_flow" target="global_bond_inflation::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in bilateral trade and investment activity raises short-term transport and industrial fuel demand (and logistic bottlenecks), directly increasing crude oil demand and lifting oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_china_india</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_inflation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_china_india::trade_investment_flow" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::crude_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in China–India trade and energy procurement directly raises tanker liftings from Persian Gulf exporters, physically increasing the barrels per day transiting regional chokepoints (e.g., Strait of Hormuz).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_china_india</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
