<edge source="brics_china_india::policy_coordination_stre" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::shipping_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">1</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger China–India policy coordination to provide diplomatic protection, coordinated state-backed insurance or organized convoy/escort arrangements reduces insurers' perceived exposure and thus lowers the incremental shipping risk premium on Gulf-to-Asia routes.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_china_india</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_china_india::policy_coordination_stre" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_support_burden" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger, coordinated BRICS diplomacy that blocks or weakens sanctions enforcement and export controls prolongs the conflict by sustaining Russian sustainment pathways, forcing external supporters to maintain or raise military and humanitarian aid budgets and thus increasing their fiscal burden.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_china_india</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_china_india::policy_coordination_stre" target="us_allied_tech_rivalry::regulatory_activity_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger coordinated BRICS policy moves (e.g., harmonized data, export or standard-setting actions) produce concrete cross-border policy pressure that prompts US-allied governments to increase legislative and regulatory activity to protect domestic firms and maintain tech controls.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_china_india</data>
  <data key="d40">us_allied_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
