<edge source="global_bond_inflation::inflation_expectations" target="brics_china_india::policy_coordination_stre" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising global inflation expectations increase domestic political and policy pressure on BRICS members to prioritize national inflation control and protective measures, reducing their willingness and bandwidth to negotiate and implement coordinated multilateral policies.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_china_india</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::inflation_expectations" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::shipping_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising inflation expectations prompt insurers and P&amp;I clubs to raise premiums and add surcharges to cover anticipated higher claims and replacement costs, increasing the per-unit shipping risk premium for oil shipments through the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
