<edge source="global_bond_inflation::oil_price_level" target="brics_china_india::trade_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in crude oil prices raises shipping, input and energy costs for exporters and importers, directly depressing bilateral trade volumes and raising transaction costs for China–India commercial flows and broader BRICS trade.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_china_india</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::oil_price_level" target="iran_gulf_chokepoints::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher oil prices raise the value of rents and sanction-leverage for Gulf producers and non-state actors, enabling greater funding and incentive to conduct maritime harassment or attacks on shipping to extract concessions or signal power, thereby increasing hostile incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_and_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher crude prices raise energy-exporting states' fiscal and FX receipts (notably Russia), enabling larger direct procurement and stockpiling of munitions and spare parts and reducing the need to pause purchases, thereby increasing the volume of weapons and material flowing into the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_support_burden" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising oil prices increase import bills and inflation for energy‑importing donor states, tightening their budgets and making each tranche of military and humanitarian assistance a larger fiscal burden for external supporters.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
