<edge source="global_bond_inflation::long_term_gov_yield" target="brics_china_india::trade_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in advanced-economy long-term government yields re-prices global safe assets and triggers rapid portfolio reallocation away from emerging-market exposures, causing immediate capital outflows and a drop in cross-border financing and FDI that reduces trade and investment flows to China and India.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_china_india</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::long_term_gov_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_and_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields raises the effective cost of financing for donor governments and defense procurement, prompting budgetary re‑prioritization or delay of large transfers and thereby reducing the near‑term volume and tempo of weapons and aid deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_inflation::long_term_gov_yield" target="us_allied_tech_rivalry::commercialization_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long-term sovereign yields raise the discount rate and depress startup valuations and exit prospects, reducing VC and corporate M&amp;A funding that directly finances productization and market rollouts of AI, slowing commercialization.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_inflation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_allied_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
